			<div class="content" id="post-content-4671505">
									

<p>If you're just interested in the link to the Sandbox demo page, it's right at the bottom of this post.<br />
So you know the scrambley text stuff Minecraft has, where it just kinda goes crazy?</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Friendly&nbsp;collapsible&nbsp;for&nbsp;Mobile&nbsp;users</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Thanks&nbsp;for&nbsp;being&nbsp;nice,&nbsp;JaonHax!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<div class="image-container alignleft"><img src="https://gamepedia.cursecdn.com/minecraft_gamepedia/thumb/7/7e/Minecraft_Formatting.gif/200px-Minecraft_Formatting.gif?version=14d34015f6cdd3412acabdd0d80764d9" alt="200px-Minecraft_Formatting.gif?version=14d34015f6cdd3412acabdd0d80764d9" class="image" /></div>
<p>(that stuff next to the k)</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Yeah, that stuff. First and foremost, I'm going to clear something up: this effect is called obfuscation and I'm going to be referring to it as such. It's a fantastic word and needs to be used more often.</p>
<p>So I dabble in a bit of programming, and recently that's extended to JavaScript, CSS and HTML because of the SCP Wiki. In the process of attempting to create something else, I was looking on Google and may or may not have found enough out to cobble together an obfuscator that can not only replicate the Minecraft style fairly closely, it can display multiple <em>different</em> messages in a sequence, has variable speed and delay times, etc.</p>
<p>I've done my best to make it user-friendly, and will continue to do so. If any issues arise with it, feel free to PM me on Wikidot. My only request is that (at least for the foreseeable future) you credit me if you make a page using it. As you can see, I'm not the most known of users on the wiki and any form of publicity here would be appreciated.</p>
<p>Alright, <a href="http://scp-sandbox-3.wikidot.com/jaonhax:obfuscator-demos-and-source">here's the link</a>, sorry for keeping you.</p>
<p><span style="font-size:60%;"><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Ungrateful bastards&#8230;</span></span> I mean &quot;lovely people!'</p>

							</div>

